**EXHIBIT A: POWER GENERATION AND DISTRIBUTION CONTRACT**

**THIS POWER GENERATION AND DISTRIBUTION CONTRACT** (the "Contract") is made as of the 1st day of March, 2023 (the "Effective Date"), by and between **Green Horizon Electric LLC**, a limited liability company registered in the State of California with its principal place of business at 123 Renewable Way, San Diego, CA 92101 (hereinafter referred to as "GHE"), and **SunPower Utilities, Inc.**, a corporation organized under the laws of the State of California with its principal office located at 456 Energy Blvd, Los Angeles, CA 90001 (hereinafter referred to as "SPU"). GHE and SPU may collectively be referred to as the "Parties" or individually as a "Party."

**WHEREAS**, GHE is engaged in the business of developing, constructing, and operating renewable power generation facilities, specifically solar photovoltaic (PV) installations;

**WHEREAS**, SPU is a utility company focused on the distribution of electric power and has the necessary infrastructure to deliver electricity to end-users in the Greater Los Angeles area;

**WHEREAS**, the Parties wish to enter into this Contract to outline the terms and conditions under which GHE will generate electricity and deliver it to SPU for distribution to its customers;

**NOW, THEREFORE**, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein, the Parties agree as follows:

### ARTICLE I: DEFINITIONS

**1.1 "Generation Facility"** means the solar PV power generation facility to be constructed and operated by GHE at 789 Solar Drive, Riverside, CA 92504, with a total capacity of 15 Megawatts (MW).

**1.2 "Delivery Point"** means the point at which electricity generated by the Generation Facility is transferred to SPU's grid infrastructure, specifically located at the SPU Riverside Substation.

**1.3 "Term"** refers to the duration of this Contract, which shall commence on the Effective Date and continue for a period of twenty (20) years, unless terminated earlier in accordance with the provisions of this Contract.

### ARTICLE II: OBLIGATIONS OF GHE

**2.1 Construction and Operation.** GHE shall be responsible for the design, construction, commissioning, and operational management of the Generation Facility, ensuring compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local laws, regulations, and permits.

**2.2 Generation Capacity.** GHE agrees to provide SPU with a minimum of 12 MW of generated electricity from the Generation Facility during the peak demand hours, defined as 12 PM to 6 PM, Monday through Friday.

**2.3 Maintenance.** GHE shall maintain the Generation Facility in accordance with industry standards and shall conduct regular inspections, with reports provided to SPU quarterly.

### ARTICLE III: OBLIGATIONS OF SPU

**3.1 Purchase of Electricity.** SPU agrees to purchase all electricity generated and delivered by GHE at the Delivery Point, subject to the terms of this Contract.

**3.2 Payment Terms.** SPU shall compensate GHE at a rate of $0.08 per kilowatt-hour (kWh) for all electricity purchased under this Contract. Payments shall be made monthly, within thirty (30) days of receipt of GHE's invoice.

**3.3 Grid Infrastructure.** SPU shall ensure that its grid infrastructure at the Riverside Substation is capable of receiving the electricity generated by the Generation Facility and shall provide any necessary upgrades or maintenance as needed.

### ARTICLE IV: REVENUE SHARING

**4.1 Renewable Energy Credits (RECs).** GHE shall retain ownership of all Renewable Energy Credits generated from the electricity produced by the Generation Facility. GHE shall have the right to sell or trade these RECs independently.

**4.2 Profit Sharing.** Should GHE achieve generation capacity exceeding 15 MW due to performance enhancements or upgrades made after the Effective Date, SPU shall receive 10% of the net profits from the sale of excess electricity.

### ARTICLE V: TERM AND TERMINATION

**5.1 Term.** The Term of this Contract shall begin on the Effective Date and shall continue for twenty (20) years unless otherwise terminated per this Article.

**5.2 Termination for Cause.** Either Party may terminate this Contract for cause upon thirty (30) days' written notice if the other Party fails to perform its obligations hereunder and such failure is not cured within the thirty (30) day notice period.

**5.3 Termination for Convenience.** Either Party may terminate this Contract for convenience upon one hundred eighty (180) days' written notice to the other Party.

### ARTICLE VI: LIABILITY AND INDEMNIFICATION

**6.1 Limitation of Liability.** Neither Party shall be liable to the other for any indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages arising out of or related to this Contract, including but not limited to loss of profits or revenues, even if such damages were foreseeable.

**6.2 Indemnification.** Each Party agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other Party, its officers, directors, employees, and agents from any and all claims, liabilities, damages, and expenses (including reasonable attorney's fees) arising out of or related to its breach of this Contract.

### ARTICLE VII: GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION

**7.1 Governing Law.** This Contract shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of California without regard to its conflict of laws principles.

**7.2 Dispute Resolution.** Any disputes arising out of or relating to this Contract shall first be addressed through good-faith negotiations between the Parties. If such negotiations do not resolve the dispute within thirty (30) days, the Parties agree to submit the dispute to mediation in Los Angeles, California. If mediation fails, the Parties may pursue any available legal remedies in a court of competent jurisdiction.

### ARTICLE VIII: MISCELLANEOUS

**8.1 Entire Agreement.** This Contract constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties and supersedes all prior negotiations, representations, or agreements, whether written or oral.

**8.2 Amendment.** This Contract may only be amended or modified by a written agreement signed by both Parties.

